      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T13:57:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This reuses the server\u0027s request-body limit (256 KiB) as the client\u0027s SSE line limit. With default fragmentation the server sends a whole notification as one line, so any notification over 256 KiB now closes the stream and the listener only sees onStreamEnd(). Could we use a dedicated, larger (or configurable) client limit instead of HTTPServerLimits.DEFAULT?",
      "revId": "c4da4c638fedcadbe4a8585ab53742b9835ea404",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
